# Real-Time Fraud Detection Engine on HPC Cloud

## Overview

The Real-Time Fraud Detection Engine on HPC Cloud is a distributed fraud detection platform designed to simulate how modern financial institutions detect fraudulent transactions in real time. The project combines **High Performance Computing (HPC), Machine Learning, DevOps, and Cybersecurity to build a scalable and secure transaction processing system.

Instead of relying on a large production cluster, the system is deployed on a 3-node HPC environment consisting of one master node and two compute nodes, making it suitable for academic demonstrations while preserving real-world architecture.

-> Project Objectives

- Build a secure HPC cluster for distributed processing.
- Stream banking transactions in real time.
- Detect fraudulent transactions using an AI model.
- Provide live monitoring and alerting dashboards.
- Automate deployment using a CI/CD pipeline.
- Demonstrate enterprise-grade security and backup strategies.

